  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Get open on the wing – V-cut and L-cut",
  "description": "Three players per basket: a passer with the ball at the top outside the three-point line, an attacker on the wing and a defender who plays tight and denies the pass. The attacker has to get open. With a V-cut the attacker walks in towards the block, taking the defender along, plants a foot and explodes back out to the wing with a hand up as a target. With an L-cut the attacker starts on the block, walks up the side of the lane to elbow height and then cuts flat out to the wing.\n\nAfter the catch the attacker squares up to the basket in triple threat (shoot, dribble or pass) and plays 1v1. Rotation: passer becomes attacker, attacker becomes defender, defender joins the back of the line behind the passer.\n\nEasier: the defender only denies and the play ends on the catch. Harder: the passer may only pass when the attacker is clearly open; otherwise the cut starts again. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Slow in, fast out – the change of speed is what gets you open."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Plant the outside foot hard on the turn and take the defender with you before you come out."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Show a clear target hand and come to meet the ball – don't wait for it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Land in triple threat with your eyes on the basket before you choose shot, drive or pass."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
